it` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) on host `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 7900X3D, Intel Arc A770 16GB), covering commits b10146\u2192b12321 (2026-09-26 to 10-01). Context A (Opus 5.5) ran 09-26\u219209-28 with the i915 driver; Context B (Sonnet 5.5) resumed 10-01 with the A770 switched to the **xe** driver by other sessions.\n\n- **Major technical work**: The session addressed a PKGBUILD rework, an LLAMA_SUBPROCESS ABI trap introduced by commit d37dd50bb, SYCL graph support, a oneDNN A/B comparison, a oneAPI 2026.0\u21922026.1 swap (DLE swap), PR #63 benchmark review, an IGC crash on DG2 XMX-gather (patched in 4e7400c3a), 256-GRF kernels, and a \"12-vs-18 t/s decode investigation.\"\n\n- **Driver change**: The A770 was bound to the **xe** kernel driver (in kernel `7.3.0-rc5-273-linux73-tkg-bore-rc5-xe`) rather than i915, a switch made by other sessions between the two contexts.\n\n- **Deliverables**: Produced a complete session"}